def disclaimer_message() -> str:
    return ("\n---------DISCLAIMER---------\nAS NOTED IN THE LICENSE, ALLIANCE FOR ENERGY INNOVATION, LLC: (i) DISCLAIMS ANY WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,"
            " INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO ANY IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE OR NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND (ii) "
            "DOES NOT ASSUME ANY LEGAL LIABILITY OR RESPONSIBILITY FOR THE ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, OR USEFULNESS OF SOFTWARE OR ITS OUTPUTS. ANY RELIANCE BY"
            " THE USER ON THE SOFTWARE IS DONE AT THE USER’S OWN RISK.\n\nBlendPATH was developed to provide the user with economic analytical capabilities "
            "to evaluate potential natural gas pipeline modifications for accommodating hydrogen blending or pure hydrogen streams and to assess the potential"
            " associated economic impacts. This model is intended for use during the early stages of pipeline repurposing concept evaluation, which is defined"
            " here as the initial project phase when the developer has already gathered the relevant pipeline material design and operation data but has not"
            " yet conducted the detailed pipeline materials testing, as specified in ASME B31.12 and/or ASTM D2837 with ASTM D2513, or performed the in-line"
            " inspections that qualify a given pipeline section for hydrogen or hydrogen blending service. Despite BlendPATH using ASME B31.12 and ASTM D2837"
            " to assess existing natural gas pipelines and establish potential pipeline modifications for a natural gas pipeline network to meet ASME B31.12"
            " and ASTM D2837/D2513 design requirements, BlendPATH does not qualify the examined pipeline network or modifications thereof for pure hydrogen "
            "or hydrogen blending. Pipeline owners and operators must conduct additional evaluations as specified in ASME B31.12, ASTM D2837 with ASTM D2513 "
            "and other relevant code and regulations, independent of BlendPATH application, to qualify actual natural gas pipelines for operation with hydrogen. "
            "Failure to do so may result in pipeline fatigue and/or rupture. It is the sole responsibility of the pipeline owner and operator to ensure that "
            "their pipeline qualifies for the ASME B31.12 design option and/or ASTM D2837 design factor (with validated ASTM D2837 hydrostatic design basis "
            "reflecting the intended gas service desired) that they choose, follows any other relevant code and regulations, and that any defects present in "
            "the pipeline are acceptable at the operating pressure chosen. Additionally, it is the responsibility of the pipeline owner and operator to ensure "
            "that other chosen operating conditions (e.g. gas velocity) do not compromise pipeline integrity. \n----------------------------\n")
